This directory must exist (even empty) before EDM4U (External Dependency Manager for
Unity) runs its Android Resolver. Its GradleTemplateResolver.EnsureGradleTemplateEnabled
copies mainTemplate.gradle from the Unity Editor's own template folder into this exact
path, and that copy throws System.IO.DirectoryNotFoundException -- silently aborting the
*entire* dependency resolution, with no build-time error -- if the directory doesn't
already exist. Confirmed by decompiling a built APK's dex and finding none of the
Play Services classes RoasAndroidBridge.cs reflects into, tracing back through
~/Library/Logs/Unity/Editor.log to this exact exception.

Everything EDM4U generates into this folder (mainTemplate.gradle, etc.) is gitignored --
only this placeholder is tracked, so the directory survives a fresh clone.
